@startuml deadlock-prevention
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FEF9C3
skinparam noteBorderColor #CA8A04
skinparam participantBorderColor #334155
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9

title Dijkstra's Resource Hierarchy — Mathematical Deadlock Freedom

participant "Philosopher-0\n(Socrates)\nleft=0, right=1" as P0 #EFF6FF
participant "EnvironmentAgent\n(Resource Authority)" as Env #F0FDF4
participant "Philosopher-4 (Last)\n(Kant)\nleft=4, right=0" as P4 #EFF6FF

autonumber

== 1. Resource Hierarchy Ordering: min(left, right) then max(left, right) ==
note over P0
  **Socrates (ID: 0):**
  firstFork  = min(0, 1) = **Fork 0**
  secondFork = max(0, 1) = **Fork 1**
end note

note over P4
  **Kant (ID: 4 - Last Philosopher):**
  firstFork  = min(4, 0) = **Fork 0**  <-- SYMMETRY BREAK!
  secondFork = max(4, 0) = **Fork 4**
end note

== 2. Both Compete for Fork 0 as Their FIRST Fork ==
P0 -> Env : **ACL: REQUEST**\nreply-with: "req-p0-f0"\ncontent: ""FORK_REQUEST:0"" [firstFork]
activate Env
P4 -> Env : **ACL: REQUEST**\nreply-with: "req-p4-f0"\ncontent: ""FORK_REQUEST:0"" [firstFork]

note over Env
  Both P0 and P4 compete for **Fork 0** as their first resource.
  Fork 0 is granted to P0 (Socrates).
  P4 (Kant) is queued with **WAIT:0**.
end note

Env --> P0 : **ACL: AGREE**\nin-reply-to: "req-p0-f0"\ncontent: ""FORK_GRANTED:0""
Env --> P4 : **ACL: INFORM**\nin-reply-to: "req-p4-f0"\ncontent: ""WAIT:0""
deactivate Env

note over P4
  **Crucial Invariant:**
  Kant holds **ZERO** forks while waiting for Fork 0.
  Kant cannot hold Fork 4 and wait for Fork 0!
end note

== 3. Progress Guarantee & No Circular Wait ==
P0 -> Env : **ACL: REQUEST**\nreply-with: "req-p0-f1"\ncontent: ""FORK_REQUEST:1"" [secondFork]
activate Env
Env --> P0 : **ACL: AGREE**\nin-reply-to: "req-p0-f1"\ncontent: ""FORK_GRANTED:1""
deactivate Env

note over P0
  P0 holds both forks (0, 1) and **EATS**.
  Deadlock is impossible because circular wait is broken.
end note

P0 -> Env : **ACL: INFORM**\ncontent: ""RELEASE_FORK:0:0""
activate Env
note over Env
  Fork 0 is released!
  Now granted to queued P4 (Kant).
end note
Env --> P4 : **ACL: AGREE**\ncontent: ""FORK_GRANTED:0""
deactivate Env

note over P0, P4
  **Theorem (Dijkstra):**
  All philosophers acquire forks in global ascending resource order:
  min(left, right) -> max(left, right)
  
  At most N-1 philosophers can acquire their first fork simultaneously.
  The resource dependency graph is a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG).
  Therefore, circular wait and deadlock cannot occur.
end note

@enduml
